# actions.mca — TikTok Events → Minecraft Commands
# For more info see GUIDE.md
# Gift IDs: see core/gifts.json

# =====================================================================
#  FOLLOW — triggers when someone follows your TikTok account
# =====================================================================

# Give every player 7 golden apples as a follow reward,
# AND show an overlay notification on stream for 5 seconds.
# The ; chains both commands: first the /give, then the >> overlay.
# {user} is automatically replaced with the follower's TikTok name.
follow:/give @a minecraft:golden_apple 7; >>New Follower!|{user} is now following you!|5

# =====================================================================
#  JOIN — triggers when a viewer joins the live stream
# =====================================================================

# This fires for EVERY join — can be very frequent on active streams.
# Use with caution: avoid expensive or spammy commands here.
# The example below is disabled (#). Remove the # to activate it.
# Show a welcome overlay when someone joins the stream.
# {user} is replaced with the viewer's TikTok username.
#join:>>Welcome!|{user} just joined the stream!|3

# =====================================================================
#  COMMENT — triggers on every comment in the live chat
# =====================================================================

# This fires for EVERY comment — can be very frequent on active streams.
# Use with caution: avoid expensive or spammy commands here.
# The example below is disabled (#). Remove the # to activate it.
# You can use {comment} to show the comment text in the overlay:
#comment:>>{user} wrote:|{comment}|3

# =====================================================================
#  LIKES — triggers based on accumulated like count
# =====================================================================

# "likes" fires every N likes (default: every 100, configured in config.yaml).
# This spawns 2 Creepers at every player's position.
# x2 = repeat the summon command 2 times = 2 Creepers.
likes:/execute at @a run summon minecraft:creeper ~ ~ ~ x2

# "like_2" fires at a bigger milestone (default: every 100_000 likes).
# First clears every player's inventory, then kills all players.
# The ; chains both commands: /clear runs first, then /kill.
like_2:/clear @a *; /kill @a

# =====================================================================
#  GIFTS — triggered by specific TikTok gift IDs
#  (find all IDs in core/gifts.json)
# =====================================================================

# --- Rose (Gift ID: 5655) ---
# Spawns 2 TNT at the player "Notch" using the DelayedTNT plugin.
# !tnt is a server plugin command (not vanilla Minecraft).
# Parameters: !tnt <Amount> <Delay> <Fuse> <Player>
#   Amount = 2      → spawn 2 TNT blocks
#   Delay  = 0.1    → 0.1 seconds between each TNT spawn
#   Fuse   = 2      → each TNT explodes after 2 seconds
#   Player = Notch  → TNT spawns at this player's position
5655:!tnt 2 0.1 2 Notch

# --- Mamma Mia (Gift ID: 16111) ---
# Gives every player 1 diamond. Simple vanilla /give command.
16111:/give @a minecraft:diamond

# --- Rosa (Gift ID: 8913) ---
# Summons 3 Evokers at every player's position.
# /execute at @a run ... = run the command at each player's location.
# x3 = repeat 3 times = 3 Evokers per player.
8913:/execute at @a run summon minecraft:evoker ~ ~ ~ x3

# --- Corgi (Gift ID: 6267) ---
# Spawns 600 TNT using the DelayedTNT plugin (massive explosion!).
# Same syntax as above: !tnt <Amount> <Delay> <Fuse> <Player>
6267:!tnt 600 0.1 2 Notch

# --- Money Gun (Gift ID: 7168) ---
# Summons 50 Withers at every player's position.
# x50 = repeat 50 times = 50 Withers.
7168:/execute at @a run summon minecraft:wither ~ ~ ~ x50

# =====================================================================
#  SPECIAL FUNCTIONS ($)
# =====================================================================

# --- Flower Show (Gift ID: 16071) ---
# $random picks one random action from all defined triggers above
# and executes it. Triggers containing $random are always excluded.
# Additional exclusions are configurable in config.yaml under:
#   Gifts > random_exclude (default: likes, like_2, follow)
16071:$random

# =====================================================================
# Trigger Name instead of ID
# =====================================================================

# You can also use trigger names instead of numeric IDs.
# It you trigger name has spaces, enclose it in single quotes ('').
# The example below defines a trigger named "Tom the Tomato" for the same gift ID 16379.
# When you define trigger name and trigger ID for the same action, the name takes priority.
# This example below executes then the Gift was sent
'Tom the Tomato':$random
# As long as the example above is active, the trigger name "Tom the Tomato" will take priority 
# over the numeric ID 16379.
# So the example below will never be executed.
16379:$random